Computational extraction of selected pyimfcs routines by Aurelien Barbotin.
Original software copyright retained; GPL-3.0 terms are reproduced in LICENSE.
The repository setup classifier says MIT, but its actual LICENSE is GPL-3.0;
this extraction follows the actual GPL-3.0 licence, not the conflicting classifier.

Experimental movie and image-domain cell outlines:
Barbotin A., Billaudeau C., Sezgin E., Carballido-Lopez R., 2024,
Quantification of membrane fluidity in bacteria using TIR-FCS: Research data.
Zenodo11236214, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11236214 .
Creative Commons Attribution4.0 International:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ .
Changes: lossless movie conversion TIFF to batch-first NPZ; cell labels losslessly
converted int32 to uint8. No spatial/temporal resampling or new sensor noise.

The multi-tau register arithmetic is adapted from multipletau0.4.1.
